#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:0
msgid ""
"Change the default terminal emulator that opens when you press Ctrl+Alt+T on "
"Ubuntu Desktop 25.04 and later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:7
msgid "Topics: Customization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:11
msgid "Change the default terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:13
msgid ""
"The default terminal, or terminal emulator, is the application that opens "
"when you press {kbd}`Ctrl+Alt+T`. If multiple terminal emulators are "
"installed, you can configure which one is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:16
msgid ""
"This is the current way to set your default terminal on Ubuntu 25.04 and "
"later. If you're using an earlier Ubuntu release, such as 24.04 LTS, switch "
"the version of this guide to 24.04."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:19
msgid ""
"Your terminal might enable you to set it as default in the terminal "
"settings. Look for a button similar to {guilabel}`Set as default terminal` "
"in the application preferences. The button might be located in the "
"*Behavior* or *General* section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:21
msgid ""
"If your terminal doesn't have such settings, enter its XDG Desktop "
"identifier in the `~/.config/ubuntu-xdg-terminals.list` file. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:26
msgid "Terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:27
msgid "Identifier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:28
msgid "Ptyxis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:29
msgid "`org.gnome.Ptyxis.desktop:new-window`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:30
msgid "GNOME Terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:31
msgid "`org.gnome.Terminal.desktop`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:32
msgid "GNOME Console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:33
msgid "`org.gnome.Console.desktop`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:34
msgid "Alacritty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:35
msgid "`Alacritty.desktop`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:36
msgid "Kitty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:37
msgid "`kitty.desktop`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:40
msgid "If the file lists multiple terminals, the first line takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/change-the-default-terminal.md:43
msgid ""
"If you're not using the standard Ubuntu GNOME desktop, the name of the "
"configuration file is different. For details, see the `xdg-terminal-exec` "
"man page."
msgstr ""
